<!-- ══ FIRST TRIP ══ -->
<!-- An opinionated plan instead of a list of categories: first-time visitors mostly want
     to be told what to do, and each day links deep into the guide. -->
<section class="sec sec-white" id="first-time">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="ft-head">
      <span class="label">First time in Milos</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Three days, if that's all you have</h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Swap the days around to suit the wind. The box above tells you which coast is calm.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="ft-days">
      <li class="ft-day">
        <span class="ft-n">Day 1</span>
        <h3 class="ft-title">The north coast and Plaka</h3>
        <p>
          Get to <a href="/beaches/sarakiniko/">Sarakiniko</a> before nine, while the white
          rock is still cool and the car park is half empty. Then
          <a href="/beaches/papafragas/">Papafragas</a>, a narrow inlet between cliffs on
          the road east, and lunch by the water in
          <a href="/villages/pollonia/">Pollonia</a>. In the evening drive up to
          <a href="/villages/plaka/">Plaka</a>, climb to the
          <a href="/sights/kastro-plaka/">Kastro</a> for sunset and eat in the lanes below.
        </p>
        <p class="ft-tip">Skip the north if the meltemi is blowing. Sarakiniko gets dangerous in big waves.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="ft-day">
        <span class="ft-n">Day 2</span>
        <h3 class="ft-title">Kleftiko by boat</h3>
        <p>
          There is no road to the south-west tip, so a full day on a boat from Adamas is the
          only way to swim into the caves and arches of
          <a href="/beaches/kleftiko/">Kleftiko</a>. Book a day or two ahead in summer, and
          keep a back-up day free: tours get cancelled when the sea is rough.
        </p>
        <p class="ft-tip">The wind box above says whether today is a boat day.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="ft-day">
        <span class="ft-n">Day 3</span>
        <h3 class="ft-title">The south beaches and old Milos</h3>
        <p>
          The south coast stays calm when the north is wild.
          <a href="/beaches/firiplaka/">Firiplaka</a> is the easy one with sand and a beach
          bar, <a href="/beaches/tsigrado/">Tsigrado</a> next door is down a rope and a
          ladder, and <a href="/beaches/paleochori/">Paleochori</a> has warm water bubbling
          up from the seabed. Late afternoon, see the
          <a href="/sights/catacombs/">catacombs</a> and the
          <a href="/sights/ancient-theater/">ancient theatre</a>, then walk down to the
          boathouses of <a href="/villages/klima/">Klima</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

